1. If the JWT containing sensitive information is generated by an untrusted source or stored insecurely (e.g., plaintext), it could be vulnerable to tampering. Attackers might manipulate the JWT to gain unauthorized access to the system or steal sensitive data, which relates to CWE-287 (Insecure Data Storage). However, this vulnerability is not directly caused by the provided code but rather how the token is managed before and after its creation/decoding.

