The primary security concern here is **CWE-184: Insecure Logging of Sensitive Data (Insecure Log Management)**. When logging user input, especially sensitive information like personal identifiers or passwords, it can lead to data breaches if the logs are accessed by unauthorized individuals. In this case, the application could be logging potentially sensitive data that an attacker might gain access to through log analysis.

Given that the input is being logged directly without any checks, the severity of this vulnerability is high. The exploitability is also high because it depends on the security of the logging system itself and whether logs can be accessed by unauthorized users.

