The function `getPickleData` directly deserializes input using `pickle.loads`, which can execute arbitrary code if the serialized data was crafted maliciously. This is known as a Deserialization of Untrusted Data (CWE-502).

Additionally, while not explicitly visible in this snippet, the use of `pickle` for serializing or deserializing any data should be avoided due to its inherent security risks. It does not support secure serialization mechanisms like JSON and can lead to remote code execution if used improperly.

