- CWE-327 (Plaintext Storage): The function directly exports the private key as OpenSSH format string which can potentially expose sensitive information if the data is leaked. This should be handled securely by ensuring that this key storage and transport process occurs over an encrypted channel, not just insecure unsecured channels.

- CWE-326 (Inadequate Encryption Strength): The size of 1024 bit RSA key may seem sufficient for most applications but it could be less secure against brute force attacks and more prone to computational cost than larger keys which may provide a trade-off.

